-For the uniform-audit baselines with refund-and-ban enforcement and no bonds, free replacement removes the ban's continuation cost. At the fixed parameters, the prescribed D2+H3 searches yield a lower measured gain for R3 than for B3 on every sampled market, but the registered gain-and-efficiency comparison passes on only three of six fresh markets, all three qualified by search flags. R3 and the development-selected verified-history comparator are pooled-equivalent within the pre-set margin in the six sampled markets under both Q1 families, which are close to one test; across markets the difference varies in sign, and the ordering is not established for the neighbourhood. At the headline market, the selected unconstrained welfare attacks yield gross efficiency of about \site{c_w0} against all three core rules and earn less than the truthful reference against R3 and C$^*$. The registered W1 search yields gross efficiency near \site{c_w1} for both rules. Exploratory episode-level mixtures selected on the evaluation records yield, with H4, estimated efficiencies of \site{c_mx_r3} for R3 and \site{c_mx_cs} for C$^*$; public D2+H3 mixtures meeting the empirical training constraint yield \site{c_mx_r3_p} and \site{c_mx_cs_p}, respectively; all at non-negative estimated evaluation gain. The registered W1 search therefore supplies no efficiency bound for randomised policies; the population profitability of the selected mixtures remains unestablished. These conclusions concern frozen searches and references, with interval calibration admitted on development fixtures. The record of both tests, including the original failure, the amendments, the deviations, and the failed predictions, will be released with the paper.
